MODULE 9 — Reductionism Fails Here (the 0/0 theorem)

A scalar solver told `x² = z²` writes `x²−z² = 0` and divides:

```
(x⁴−z⁴)/(x²−z²) = x²+z²        ← undefined exactly when the gate holds
```

The identity is true precisely when the division is undefined. Gate-firing and `0/0` are the same event, in every module:

